rd.py) is enforced via `make lint` and only scans src/rebar, so it does NOT cover test modules — the dead-stamp test's line-4 `import fcntl` is genuinely unguarded and outside that gate's scope"],"finding":"The plan does not enumerate the existing deterministic fcntl-import gate (scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py, run by `make lint`, tested by tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py) as a related consumer/context. That gate is scoped to src/rebar modules and its regression test already documents that `import rebar` is collectable without fcntl — which partly contradicts the plan's suspected-root-cause framing and is the nearest existing precedent for the collection-guard pattern the plan proposes for a test module.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1beef7f9137b3224","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Suspected root cause / Plan step 2 (Windows collection guard)","norm_id":"n5eebb6a62475b959","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author assumes the existing fcntl gate already prevents this class of Windows collection break and is surprised it does not cover test modules","Reviewer expects the plan to reuse the established try/except or sys.platform guard idiom that the existing gate's test enumerates as collection-safe"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_